@page "/mcp-server"

@* Describes the MCP server this demo's host maps at /mcp. Its route differs from the endpoint's on
   purpose: two literal endpoints on /mcp would make a GET of it ambiguous. *@

<PageTitle>MCP server - bit Bortable</PageTitle>

<div class="demo-header">
    <h3>MCP server</h3>
    <p class="text-muted">
        This site hosts a Model Context Protocol server at <code>/mcp</code>, so an AI agent writing sortable-list,
        kanban and drag-and-drop code with Bit.Bortable reads the library itself - its compiled API documentation,
        its guide, its stylesheet and these demo pages - instead of guessing at an API it half remembers, or
        borrowing one from SortableJS. Every tool is read-only.
    </p>
</div>

<section class="mcp-panel">
    <h4>Connect a client</h4>

    <p>
        The endpoint is plain Streamable HTTP, so any MCP client connects with a URL and nothing else. The same tools
        are also served, version by version, through the bit platform's own server at
        <code>https://bitplatform.dev/mcp</code>, next to the other bit libraries.
    </p>

    <pre class="mcp-output"><code>@ClientConfig</code></pre>
</section>

<section class="mcp-panel">
    <h4>Tools</h4>

    <table class="mcp-table">
        <thead>
            <tr><th>Tool</th><th>What it answers</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            @foreach (var tool in Tools)
            {
                <tr>
                    <td><code>@tool.Name</code></td>
                    <td>@((MarkupString)tool.Description)</td>
                </tr>
            }
        </tbody>
    </table>

    <p>
        The guide, the API, the theme, a sample drag and the sources are also exposed as <code>bortable://</code>
        resources, and three prompts - <code>add-bortable-to-app</code>, <code>implement-bortable-feature</code> and
        <code>debug-bortable-drag</code> - walk an agent through the common jobs in the right order.
    </p>
</section>

<section class="mcp-panel">
    <h4>The same tools over plain HTTP</h4>

    <p>
        Every tool is also a <code>GET</code> under <code>/api/mcp/...</code>: open one in a browser tab to read
        exactly what an agent is handed.
    </p>

    <ul>
        @foreach (var (href, text) in HttpExamples)
        {
            <li><a href="@href" target="_blank" rel="noopener">@text</a></li>
        }
    </ul>
</section>

@* The demo's stylesheet has no panel or table styles of its own - every other page is a list - so the
   few this page needs live with it, built on the site's own --demo-* palette. *@
<style>
    .mcp-panel {
        max-width: 960px;
        margin-bottom: 1.1rem;
        padding: 1rem 1.2rem;
        border: 1px solid var(--demo-border);
        border-radius: var(--demo-radius);
        background: var(--demo-surface);
        box-shadow: var(--demo-shadow);
        line-height: 1.55;
    }

    .mcp-panel h4 {
        margin: 0 0 0.6rem;
        font-size: 1.05rem;
    }

    .mcp-panel p {
        margin: 0.4rem 0;
    }

    .mcp-panel ul {
        margin: 0.4rem 0;
        padding-left: 1.2rem;
        overflow-wrap: anywhere;
    }

    .mcp-output {
        margin: 0.6rem 0 0;
        padding: 0.8rem 1rem;
        overflow-x: auto;
        border-radius: 8px;
        background: #f1f2f4;
        font-size: 0.85rem;
    }

    .mcp-output code {
        color: var(--demo-text);
    }

    .mcp-table {
        width: 100%;
        border-collapse: collapse;
        font-size: 0.9rem;
    }

    .mcp-table th,
    .mcp-table td {
        padding: 0.45rem 0.6rem;
        border-bottom: 1px solid var(--demo-border);
        text-align: left;
        vertical-align: top;
    }

    .mcp-table td:first-child {
        white-space: nowrap;
    }

    @@media (max-width: 640.98px) {
        .mcp-table td:first-child {
            white-space: normal;
            overflow-wrap: anywhere;
        }
    }
</style>

@code {
    private const string ClientConfig = """
        // .mcp.json (Claude Code, VS Code, and anything else reading this shape)
        {
          "mcpServers": {
            "bortable": {
              "type": "http",
              "url": "https://bortable.bitplatform.dev/mcp"
            }
          }
        }
        """;

    // The server's tools, in the order an agent usually needs them. The one place to change when a tool is
    // added, renamed or retired; the description is markup.
    private static readonly (string Name, string Description)[] Tools =
    [
        ("SearchBortable",
            "Everything at once - the guide, every public type and member, the setup guides, the stylesheet's custom properties and classes and the demo's pages - each hit with the exact follow-up call."),
        ("GetBortableSetupGuide",
            "The complete wiring for one render mode: server, wasm, auto, standalone-wasm or hybrid - <code>AddBitBortableServices()</code> in every project that renders a list, the stylesheet link and an interactive render mode."),
        ("GetBortableGuideSection",
            "One section of the reference guide, or the index of sections."),
        ("GetBortableApi",
            "One public type - <code>Bortable&lt;TItem&gt;</code>, <code>BortableEventArgs&lt;TItem&gt;</code>, <code>BortablePull</code>, <code>BortableDirection</code>, <code>BitBortable</code> - with every parameter, property, method or value, its real default and its documentation, or the index of types."),
        ("GetBortableTheme",
            "The <code>--bit-bortable-*</code> custom properties - the accent and opacities declared on <code>:root</code>, and the colours the state rules read with a fallback - with their defaults and what each one paints, and the drag-state classes (<code>bit-bortable-ghost</code>, <code>bit-bortable-chosen</code>, <code>bit-bortable-hidden</code>, <code>bit-bortable-swap-highlight</code>, <code>bit-bortable-selected</code> and the rest) with the parameter that replaces each."),
        ("GetBortableSourceFile",
            "One demo page, the library's component or its stylesheet verbatim - every page here is a working list, and a page's route works as its path - or the index of files."),
        ("InspectBortableDrag",
            "Renders a real <code>Bortable&lt;string&gt;</code> for each list you describe as JSON, performs one drag through its own handlers - within a list, across lists, a clone, a swap or a multi-drag - and reports whether each step was accepted and why not, the lists before and after, and every event raised, in order, with its arguments."),
    ];

    private static readonly (string Href, string Text)[] HttpExamples =
    [
        ("/api/mcp/SearchBortable?query=drag%20handle", "/api/mcp/SearchBortable?query=drag handle"),
        ("/api/mcp/GetBortableApi?typeName=Bortable", "/api/mcp/GetBortableApi?typeName=Bortable"),
        ("/api/mcp/GetBortableTheme?name=bit-bortable-ghost", "/api/mcp/GetBortableTheme?name=bit-bortable-ghost"),
        ("/api/mcp/InspectBortableDrag", "/api/mcp/InspectBortableDrag (runs the sample drag)"),
        ("/api/mcp/InspectBortableDrag?json=%7B%22lists%22%3A%5B%7B%22id%22%3A%22todo%22%2C%22group%22%3A%22board%22%2C%22items%22%3A%5B%22Spec%22%2C%22Review%22%5D%7D%2C%7B%22id%22%3A%22done%22%2C%22group%22%3A%22board%22%2C%22put%22%3Afalse%2C%22items%22%3A%5B%5D%7D%5D%2C%22drag%22%3A%7B%22item%22%3A%22Review%22%2C%22to%22%3A%22done%22%7D%7D",
            "/api/mcp/InspectBortableDrag?json={ ... \"put\": false ... } (a refused drop, explained)"),
        ("/api/mcp/GetBortableSourceFile?path=Demo/Client/Pages/Shared.razor", "/api/mcp/GetBortableSourceFile?path=Demo/Client/Pages/Shared.razor"),
    ];
}
